/**
 * @defgroup StarAgmlViewer StarAgmlViewer — AGML Interactive Geometry Viewer
 * @brief Interactive EVE-based 3D visualisation of the AGML-assembled TGeo geometry.
 * @ingroup StarAgmlLib
 *
 * `StarAgmlViewer` integrates with the ROOT EVE (Event Visualisation
 * Environment) system to provide interactive 3D visualisation of the TGeo
 * geometry produced by `StarTGeoStacker`.  It is implemented as a `StMaker`
 * so that it can be embedded in the standard STAR maker chain.
 *
 * Key capabilities:
 * - Opens an EVE/OpenGL viewer window and imports the current `TGeoManager`
 *   tree on `Init()`.
 * - `addGlobalElement(vol, node)` — adds a specific TGeo volume/node to the
 *   EVE global scene for display in all viewer windows.
 * - `applyTransparency(TOP, mode)` — recursively sets the transparency of all
 *   volumes in the sub-tree rooted at `TOP`, making outer shells
 *   semi-transparent to reveal inner detector components.
 *
 * @par Related modules
 * - @ref StarAgmlLib    — core AGML geometry description library
 * - @ref StarAgmlUtil   — coordinate transforms and parameter utilities
 * - @ref StarAgmlChecker — material-budget analysis of the same geometry
 *
 * @{
 */

/**
 * @class StarAgmlViewer
 * @brief StMaker that opens an EVE geometry viewer for the assembled AGML/TGeo geometry.
 * @ingroup StarAgmlViewer
 *
 * On `Init()` the viewer calls `LoadGeometry()` which wraps the current
 * `gGeoManager` in a `TEveGeoTopNode` and registers it with the EVE manager,
 * enabling interactive rotation, zooming, and per-volume selection via the
 * ROOT GL viewer (`TGLViewer`).
 *
 * `addGlobalElement(vol, node)` locates a named volume in the TGeo hierarchy
 * and adds the specified daughter node as an EVE global element.
 *
 * `applyTransparency(TOP, mode)` recursively adjusts volume transparency
 * throughout the named sub-tree; `mode = -1` applies a default level suitable
 * for inspecting nested structures.
 */

/**
 * @}
 */
